Additional contributions and inspirations

https://github.com/lalinsky/dusty
Copyright (c) 2025 Lukas Lalinsky and contributors.

- The Updated accept() code with incremental backoff is taken in part directly from 
  the way that dusty does the same thing. I didnt realize that accept() has a whole range of 
  common failure modes that really need to be checked in detail and treated very differently.


https://github.com/karlseguin/http.zig
Copyright (c) 2024 Karl Seguin.

- The general concept of the server loop + router + general coding API taken mostly from
  Karl's excellent http.zig - which predates zig's std.Io. I was a pretty heavy contributor 
  to this project, and this whole datastar library initially started as an experiment to 
  port http.zig across to zig's new std.Io, by stripping it back to remove the Io loop and
  posix code.
